{
  "title": "StrRAT-AV-Discovery",
  "description": "StrRAT is a Java-based remote access tool which steals browser credentials, logs keystrokes and take remote control of infected systems. It also has a module to download additional payload onto to the infected machine based on C2 server command. Additionally, this threat also has a ransomware encryption/decryption module which appends .crimson extension.\n",
  "query": "('Log Source' = 'Microsoft Defender Endpoint Logs' or 'Log Source' = 'SOC Windows Sysmon Logs') and ('Parent Process Name' in ('java.exe', 'javaw.exe') and 'Command Line' like '*roaming*') and ('Process Name' = 'cmd.exe' and 'Command Line' like '*path antivirusproduct get displayname*')",
